  "query_preview": "..A weak ridge will remain across the region on Saturday \nbefore a trough starts to drop down from the north which will \ndominate our weather through at least the middle of next week. The \ngradient will begin to tighten up on Saturday with increasing \nsouthwest winds, mainly across western portions of the forecast \narea. With the dry conditions in place we will see critical fire \nweather conditions across western Coconino county and portions of \nYavapai county on Saturday. The trough will also bring some slightly \ncooler temperatures which will bring us back down near normal \nthrough the week.\n\nWinds will increase on Sunday with more widespread fire weather \nconcerns expected. Winds on Sunday may near Wind Advisory levels so \nsomething to keep an eye on for your weekend forecast. \n\nWinds remain breezy through at least mid-week across the state. \nTuesday looks to be the windiest day of the week so another day to \nkeep an eye on. Conditions will remain near-critical to critical \nthrough at least Tuesday, before the trough finally starts to lift \nto the north and we the gradient weakens across the region. \n\nA few outside chances for some showers towards the NM border on \nTuesday but confidence is low that we will see much if anything \nreach the ground due to the very dry conditions in place.",
